---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GlassCard from '../components/GlassCard.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'May 16, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Accessibility | BabyBlocks"
  description="BabyBlocks accessibility statement. Our standards, what we support today, known limitations, and how to report a barrier."
  canonical="/accessibility"
>
  <section class="sec-hero section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-hero-inner">
        <div class="label-chip">Accessibility</div>
        <h1>Built to be used by everyone.<br /><span class="text-gradient">Standards, support, and where we still fall short.</span></h1>
        <p>
          We design BudgetBaby, PantryBaby, and this website to be usable by as many people as possible.
          This page describes what we support today, what we are still working on, and how to tell us when we get it wrong.
        </p>
        <p class="sec-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard accent padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="target" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Our target</h2>
            <p>
              We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (<strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong>) on
              the website, and the Apple Human Interface Guidelines for accessibility on the iOS apps.
              We do not yet have a third-party audit. This statement reflects our own assessment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="check" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>What is supported today</h2>
            <h3>iOS apps (BudgetBaby and PantryBaby)</h3>
            <ul class="sec-list">
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Dynamic Type. Text scales with the system text size setting.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> VoiceOver. Every interactive element has an accessibility label.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Reduce Motion. Animations honor the system setting.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Dark Mode and Light Mode, with a manual override in app settings.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> System tinting. Interactive elements use system-managed accent colors.</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Haptic feedback for confirmation events, which respects the system haptics setting</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> All currency and date input fields work with the standard iOS keyboard, including the dictation key</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Face ID and Touch ID are optional, not required</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Website (babyblocks.io)</h3>
            <ul class="sec-list">
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Semantic HTML with proper heading order on every page</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Skip-to-content links on long pages</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Keyboard navigation across all pages, including modal sheets and forms</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Color contrast meets WCAG AA on body text and primary controls</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Forms have associated labels and clear error messages</li>
              <li><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Images that carry meaning have descriptive alt text; decorative images are marked as such</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="info" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Known limitations</h2>
            <p>We document gaps publicly. These are the issues we know about and are working on.</p>
            <ul class="sec-list muted">
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> Some hand-drawn iPhone mockups inside documentation pages are illustrative only and are not announced by screen readers. Equivalent prose appears in the same section.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> The iOS apps are currently English-only. Localized accessibility labels follow the i18n work tracked in our roadmap.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> Chart visualizations in BudgetBaby Insights do not yet have a tabular alternative. A data-table view is planned.</li>
              <li><Icon name="x-circle" size={14} /> We have not yet conducted formal testing with users who rely on Switch Control.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec-section section-sm">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <GlassCard padding="lg">
        <div class="sec-block">
          <div class="sec-block-icon"><Icon name="mail" size={28} /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Report an accessibility barrier</h2>
            <p>
              If something does not work for you, tell us. Email
              <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a> with
              <strong>[Accessibility]</strong> at the start of the subject line. We treat accessibility
              reports the same as security reports. Flagged on arrival, triaged same-day.
            </p>
            <p>
              Please include the device, the assistive technology you use, the page or screen, and what you expected to happen.
              If you can attach a screen recording, even better.
            </p>
            <p>
              We commit to acknowledging accessibility reports within two business days and providing
              a planned resolution date within ten business days.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </GlassCard>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .sec-hero { padding-top: calc(var(--space-20) + var(--space-8)); }
  .sec-hero-inner { max-width: 720px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-hero-inner h1 { font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 6vw, var(--text-6xl)); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .sec-hero-inner p { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 56ch; }
  .sec-updated { font-size: var(--text-xs) !important; color: var(--text-muted) !important; max-width: none !important; }
  .sec-section { padding-block: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block { display: flex; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-block-icon { color: var(--accent-light); flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: var(--space-1); }
  .sec-block h2 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-top: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .sec-block p { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .sec-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .sec-block a { color: var(--accent-light); text-decoration: none; }
  .sec-block a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .sec-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); padding-left: 0; }
  .sec-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-2); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .sec-list.muted li { color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
